tasks.append(r"""  () => revR('lovelock-compare', 'Revision', 'lovelock-compare', `Own ONLY the new folder ${R}/gkd_lovelock/comparison/. NEVER modify the author's notebook ${ROOT}/Pair_Creation_of_Universes_WaveFunctionOfUniverse-4+4-Einstein-Lovelock-Nash.nb or any other author notebook (read only; Get/Import of the notebook expression in WolframScript, never NotebookOpen with saving, never NotebookSave). Never quote the author's private PDF. (The progress log of this task is in ${SP}/phase2/lovelock-compare.progress.md, not in phase2b: read and append there.) Carry out and record the comparison that ${R}/gkd_lovelock/results/PROVENANCE_OF_THE_COMPUTATION.md announces but that is recorded nowhere: the Revision's curvature and Lovelock results (${R}/gkd_lovelock/results/curvature.json, lovelock-tensors.json) against the author's OWN stored outputs. The earlier run found: the notebook_reading set reads 'Generalized _Kronecker_Delta_4+4.nb' (only kdelta/GKD outputs there, no metric or Lovelock cells); the main notebook Pair_Creation_...nb has 2127 cells (996 Input, 805 Output); rt[g] at In[214] computes ginv, Christoffel, Ricci, Riemann, RS, EinsteinG; In[238] rt[gtry] (no output); stored outputs Out[235] (gtry = MatrixMetric44), Out[535] (RS), Out[536] (EinsteinG); no Lovelock P2/P3 output was found in either notebook - re-check that. Write ${R}/gkd_lovelock/comparison/extract_author_curvature_outputs.wls (read-only; converts the stored OUTPUT boxes to exact expressions WITHOUT evaluating the notebook's definitions - MakeExpression/ToExpression with HoldComplete - and writes author-curvature-outputs.json: Out labels, cell indices, exact InputForm strings, the notebook sha256, the Wolfram version; deterministic, LF), ${R}/gkd_lovelock/comparison/compare_with_author.py (sympy: state the coordinate and function mapping between the author's gtry/MatrixMetric44 and the Revision metric, check it on the metric itself FIRST; then compare the Ricci scalar and every Einstein-tensor component EXACTLY, with every normalisation stated and applied, never fitted; one check per compared object, PASS / FAIL / NOT-AVAILABLE; report author-comparison-report.json) and README.md (what was read and how, the mapping, the result, commands and run times, side effects incl. WolframScript's two tmp_* files, what the comparison does NOT establish - e.g. no author output exists for the k = 2, 3 Lovelock tensors if that is confirmed). Run each program twice: byte-identical. A disagreement is a finding: report it with the data, never hide it or change conventions after the fact. In open_items give the exact sentences the lead must change in ${R}/docs/LOVELOCK_GKD.md and results/PROVENANCE_OF_THE_COMPUTATION.md, and the index row for the new .wls.`)""")
tasks.append("  () => tbkR('fix:16', 'fix-16', " + js(E1["fix:16"]) + ").then(f => verifyFix('16', `${ROOT}/Revision/workflows/completion/review_16.json plus the 31-check cross-check update`, f)).then(v => refix('16', v))")
tasks.append("  () => tbkR('fix:17', 'fix-17', " + js(E1["fix:17"]) + ").then(f => verifyFix('17', `${ROOT}/Revision/workflows/completion/review_17.json plus the A4 SYNC and the ks_source teaching`, f)).then(v => refix('17', v))")
tasks.append(r"""  () => agent(`""" + rv19.replace("TASK (adversarial reviewer of chapter 19", "${RESUME('review19')}\\nTASK (adversarial reviewer of chapter 19") + r"""`, { label: 'review:19', phase: 'Textbook', schema: FINDINGS })
    .then(r => (r && r.findings && r.findings.length)
      ? tbkN('fix:19', `You own chapter 19 (${T}/chapters/19-t3-kohn-sham-universes.md), its notebook builders, notebooks, PROVENANCE files and figures (${T}/notebooks/src/19*.py, ${T}/notebooks/19*, ${T}/figures/19*). Reviewer findings (JSON): ${JSON.stringify(r.findings).slice(0, 60000)}\n${FIXTAIL}`)
          .then(f => verifyFix('19', `the review findings (JSON): ${JSON.stringify(r.findings).slice(0, 30000)}`, f)).then(v => refix('19', v))
      : { files_changed: [], commands_run: [], all_checks_pass: !!r, failing: r ? [] : ['review:19 returned nothing'], key_results: [r ? 'review:19: no findings' : 'review:19: no result'], open_items: [], summary: r ? 'chapter 19 reviewed without findings' : 'review 19 failed' })""")
tasks.append(r"""  () => agent(`""" + st4.replace("TASK (stage4-diagnose;", "${RESUME('stage4-diagnose')}\\nTASK (stage4-diagnose;") + r"""`, { label: 'stage4-diagnose', phase: 'Old Stage 4', schema: RESULT })
    .then(d => d ? agent(`${NOAGREE}\nCONTEXT: repository ${ROOT} (git, branch main; Windows 11; Python 3.14; Rust cargo 1.91; WolframScript). NEVER run git commands that change the index, the working tree's history or the remote (read-only git is fine). Scratch only under ${SP}/phase3a/stage4-fix/. Read files in chunks of at most 300 lines. NEVER weaken a check or a tolerance; fix causes. NEVER modify the original textbook provenance/DIRAC16COMPLEX_TEXTBOOK.* or provenance/textbook/ (preserved by the user's order of 2026-10-02) and never the author's notebooks.\n${BOUND}\nTASK (stage4-fix): Complete the OLD Stage 4 (first edition, dirac16complex Kohn-Sham) by fixing the causes found by the diagnosis below, at the root, and regenerating every stale output in dependency order: the reference code (scripts/ks_reference_*.py) and its outputs (artifacts/dirac16complex/kohn-sham/reference/, reference-summary.json; artifacts/dirac16complex/pair-creation/reference/reference-pairs-summary.json, which records stale sha256 of scripts/ks_reference_solver.py and ks_reference_pairs.py), the Python check report artifacts/dirac16complex/kohn-sham/python-check-report.json, the notebook notebooks/dirac16complex_kohn_sham.ipynb with its runner, notebook-report.json and figures, the tests (tests/test_d16c_kohn_sham_*.py must pass, without weakening), the Stage-4 documents that quote changed numbers (find them with git grep; rebuild their PDFs and re-register them in provenance/pdf-specifications.json, changing only their entries), and the execution-provenance record notebooks/dirac16complex_kohn_sham.PROVENANCE.md (update it to the new state; it must name the current sha256 of the notebook). Long runs go to the background; if the whole regeneration cannot finish within the bound, stop at a CONSISTENT state (never leave half-regenerated outputs in the repository: generate into scratch and copy in only complete, verified sets) and list exactly what remains with the commands. The diagnosis (JSON): ${JSON.stringify(d).slice(0, 40000)}`, { label: 'stage4-fix', phase: 'Old Stage 4', schema: RESULT }) : null)
    .then(f => f ? agent(`${NOAGREE}\nCONTEXT: repository ${ROOT} (git, branch main). NEVER run git commands that change the index, the working tree or the remote; do NOT edit files. Scratch only under ${SP}/phase3a/stage4-verify/.\n${BOUND}\nTASK (stage4-verify; adversarial): The old Stage-4 fixer reports (JSON): ${JSON.stringify(f).slice(0, 40000)}\nVerify every claim in the files and by running the commands yourself (in a fresh clone of the working tree's state under scratch where a run would write into the repository): the code change fixes the diagnosed cause and weakens no check or tolerance; the regenerated outputs are reproduced byte for byte by a re-run; notebook-report.json verdict and the gauntlet; python -m unittest discover -s tests -p "test_d16c_kohn_sham*.py"; the rebuilt PDFs in verify mode; the provenance record names the current sha256. Report as findings only what is wrong or unverified, with evidence.`, { label: 'stage4-verify', phase: 'Old Stage 4', schema: FINDINGS }) : null)""")
tasks.append(r"""  () => tbkN('tb-charge', `You own the chapters ${T}/chapters/00-how-to-use-this-book.md, 20-do-universes-come-in-pairs.md, 21-matter-and-antimatter.md and ${T}/chapters/abstract.md, and the builders/notebooks/PROVENANCE/figures of chapters 20 and 21 (${T}/notebooks/src/2[01]*.py, ${T}/notebooks/2[01]*, ${T}/figures/2[01]*) - NOT chapter 22 and NOT the notebooks of chapter 00. PHYSICS CORRECTION (found by the fixers of chapters 10 and 18, verified there): only the LOCAL U(1) law d_mu(cos z J^mu) = 0 is proved (lead check u1_noether_matrix_identity); the total charge of a slice is constant only if no charge flows through the brane z = pi/2 (the flow is sin z q8 with q8 = -i Psibar gamma^(x8) Psi; on the homogeneous solutions of chapter 18, Notebook 18c, q8 runs from -0.3454 to 0.3454, so the patch charge changes at the rate -V6 q8); the no-flux condition is ASSUMED or OPEN, never proved. Read chapter 18 section 18.21 and chapter 10 section 10.2 (both already corrected) first. Then correct EVERY unqualified claim of exact total-charge conservation in your files (at least chapter 00 line ~74; chapter 20 lines ~2833 and ~2842 (2787 already qualifies it); chapter 21 lines ~12, 3765, 4348, 4664, 4706, 4853 and its notebook builders such as 21b; abstract.md line ~5) - search them all (grep for 'conserved', 'conservation', 'no net charge'), qualify each precisely, keep the R3 honesty labels. Also: chapter 20 line ~2868 says Sakharov condition 2 'is not addressed', weaker than chapter 21's PROVED failure of condition 2 for the commuting field (C_+ exact, Proposition 2): align it. Rebuild every notebook whose builder you change (python ${T}/tools/nbkit.py build <builder> --date 2026-10-08) and check it; run the walk-through audit for changed notebooks (${QUOTES}); test-build each changed chapter with python ${T}/tools/check_chapter.py until chapter_check=OK with no problem= or latex_warning= lines. List every changed sentence (file, line, old -> new) in key_results. Also put into open_items the exact new wording for rule R3 of ${T}/TEXTBOOK_SPEC.md (the lead edits the spec).`)
    .then(f => agent(`${TBCOMMON}\n${STATE}\n${BOUND}\nTASK (verify-tb-charge; adversarial; do NOT edit files): A fixer qualified the claims of total U(1) charge conservation in chapters 00, 20, 21 and abstract.md (only the local law is proved; constancy needs no flux through the brane z = pi/2). Its report: ${JSON.stringify(f || {}).slice(0, 30000)}\nSearch the WHOLE book (${T}/chapters/*.md, ${T}/notebooks/src/*.py) for any remaining unqualified claim of exact total-charge conservation or 'no net charge can be generated' (report each with file and line; chapter 22 is handled by another agent - report its lines too, as one finding), check that every changed sentence is correct physics and consistent with chapters 10.2 and 18.21, re-run nbkit check for the changed notebooks and check_chapter for the changed chapters. Findings only for real problems, with evidence.`, { label: 'verify-tb-charge', phase: 'Textbook', schema: FINDINGS }))""")
tasks.append(r"""  () => tbkN('tb-22-dark', `You own chapter 22 (${T}/chapters/22-open-problems.md) and its notebook builders/notebooks/PROVENANCE/figures (${T}/notebooks/src/22*.py, ${T}/notebooks/22*, ${T}/figures/22*). (1) The dark-sector hypotheses are no longer 'being investigated, no results claimed': the Revision record now has results (${R}/dark_sector/dirac16complex and dirac16complex00: READMEs, outputs, reports; ${R}/docs/DARK_SECTOR_HYPOTHESES.md, registered). Rewrite the chapter's dark-sector part to teach them for a student who knows school algebra: the observer assumption for rho_4 (definitions A, B, C) and how every verdict depends on it, w_eff = X/E (A, B) and X/E - 1 (C) derived line by line, the Kohn-Sham gas (radiation-like, the brane band), the condensate, mixtures, dirac16complex00's modes and populations, the Unite comparison with EVERY tuned parameter labelled CHOSEN / by construction / NOT a prediction and ghost components labelled ghost-like, and what remains open - every number read from the records. Add a new notebook 22b (builder ${T}/notebooks/src/22b_<short>.py, built with python ${T}/tools/nbkit.py build ... --date 2026-10-08) that reproduces the key dark-sector numbers from the committed Revision outputs (asserting each against its record file and check) and draws at least four teaching figures (w_eff histories under A/B/C for the gas, the condensate, a mixture, the dirac16complex00 populations against the Unite CPL line); its run-instruction paragraph, walk-through (every code line explained) and figure captions in the chapter; update the chapter's proved/computed/assumed section and exercises (with worked answers). (2) Chapter 22 line ~1919 says the U(1) charge is exactly conserved: qualify it (only the local law d_mu(cos z J^mu) = 0 is proved; constancy of the total charge needs no flux through the brane z = pi/2, ASSUMED/OPEN; see chapters 10.2 and 18.21). Then nbkit check every notebook of the chapter, the walk-through audit (${QUOTES}), and check_chapter until chapter_check=OK with no problem= or latex_warning= lines.`)
    .then(f => agent(`${TBCOMMON}\n${STATE}\n${BOUND}\nTASK (verify-tb-22; adversarial; do NOT edit files): Chapter 22 (${T}/chapters/22-open-problems.md) was rewritten to teach the Revision dark-sector results and got a new notebook 22b. Fixer report: ${JSON.stringify(f || {}).slice(0, 30000)}\nCheck every formula (re-derive w_eff for A, B, C), every number against ${R}/dark_sector/** and ${R}/docs/DARK_SECTOR_HYPOTHESES.md, the honesty labels (tuned parameters, ghosts, observer assumption, nothing established), the notebook (nbkit check), the walk-through audit, the run instructions, the figures and captions, the exercises, check_chapter. Findings only for real problems, with evidence.`, { label: 'verify-tb-22', phase: 'Textbook', schema: FINDINGS }))
    .then(v => (v && v.findings && v.findings.length) ? tbkN('refix:22', `You own chapter 22 (${T}/chapters/22-open-problems.md) and its notebooks (${T}/notebooks/src/22*.py, ${T}/notebooks/22*, ${T}/figures/22*). An adversarial verifier found (JSON): ${JSON.stringify(v.findings).slice(0, 50000)}\n${FIXTAIL}`) : v)""")

